[
    {
        "content": "<p>I would like to have both Set.Pairwise and Pairwise under a unified interface like this</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">module</span>\n\n<span class=\"n\">public</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">abbrev</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PairwiseNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Membership</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">β</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"o\">⦄,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∀</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">⦃</span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"o\">⦄,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≠</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">y</span>\n\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PairwiseOld</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">PairwiseNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">univ</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">def</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">PairwiseOld</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Set</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">r</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">α</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">→</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Prop</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">PairwiseNew</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">s</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">r</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>which is motivated by the new development here <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/More.20.60IsConcrete.60.20classes.20for.20.60SetLike.60\">#mathlib4 &gt; More &#96;IsConcrete&#96; classes for &#96;SetLike&#96;</a>  and also by my Multiset.Pairwise PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/41709\">#41709</a></p>\n<p>What do you think?</p>",
        "id": 622850952,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788962141
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Another option would be to have <code>Pairwise</code> (status quo) and <code>PairwiseMem</code> (replacing Set.Pairwise)</p>",
        "id": 622852613,
        "sender_full_name": "Eric Wieser",
        "timestamp": 1788962422
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>One thing to be aware of here is that this would mean <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Pairwise#doc\">docs#List.Pairwise</a> and <code>PairwiseNew</code> on list would differ in meaning. That's not necessarily an argument against.</p>",
        "id": 622859019,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1788963591
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I thought about that. A reason why I want the new Pairwise take the name is because you can state theorems with the new type classes coming in <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/42661\">#42661</a></p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"sd\">/-- A class to indicate that the infimum on a type corresponds to set intersection. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMemInf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Min</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The infimum corresponds to set intersection. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊓</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∧</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n\n<span class=\"kd\">@[</span><span class=\"n\">simp</span><span class=\"kd\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">alias</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">SetLike</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMemInf</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">mem_inf</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- A class to indicate that the supremum on a type corresponds to set union. -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">class</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">IsMemSup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Max</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">where</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"sd\">/-- The supremum corresponds to set union. -/</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"kn\">protected</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">mem_sup</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">A</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">B</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">↔</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">S</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∨</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">x</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">∈</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">T</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">rfl</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>all theorems are generalised for the old definitions once the new type classes arrive. And you also get theorems for Lists, Mulitsets etc. for free once you instantiate the type classes.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/Mathlib/Data/Set/Pairwise/Basic.html#Set.Pairwise.inter_left\">Set.Pairwise.inter_left</a> could be stated in terms of IsMemInf for example.</p>\n<p>Not that many theorems use the standard pairwise, and those that do are definition independent.</p>",
        "id": 622860213,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788963815
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"246273\">Bhavik Mehta</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Unification.20of.20Pairwise.20interface/near/622859019\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>One thing to be aware of here is that this would mean <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Pairwise#doc\">docs#List.Pairwise</a> and <code>PairwiseNew</code> on list would differ in meaning. That's not necessarily an argument against.</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>That's correct. List.Pairwise will be kept as is. A theorem connecting List.Pairwise will be provided for when r is symmetric on the elements on the list. But I assume such theorem is already in the library.</p>",
        "id": 622860613,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788963894
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yup, although it requires no duplicates too: <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=List.Nodup.pairwise_coe#doc\">docs#List.Nodup.pairwise_coe</a></p>",
        "id": 622865303,
        "sender_full_name": "Bhavik Mehta",
        "timestamp": 1788964766
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yeah, all theorems that are already formulated via Pairwise and Set.Pairwise will after that be intact. The big benefits will be unlocked once we get the new lattice coherence typeclasses.</p>",
        "id": 622865915,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1788964904
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>reviewing my PRs will make that go faster :)</p>",
        "id": 622915500,
        "sender_full_name": "Artie Khovanov",
        "timestamp": 1788974593
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Ok, I've started with the unification. Not completely done yet, but if there is some general feedback to it it would be nice. <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/43635\">#43635</a></p>",
        "id": 623194322,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1789055833
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Are you planning to provide an <code>abbrev</code> for <code>Set.Pairwise</code>? It would be nice so we don't lose access to dot notation.</p>",
        "id": 623214468,
        "sender_full_name": "Jireh Loreaux",
        "timestamp": 1789060910
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes.</p>",
        "id": 623214546,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1789060929
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I just want it to compile first for the _root_.Pairwise.</p>",
        "id": 623214645,
        "sender_full_name": "metakuntyyy",
        "timestamp": 1789060957
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Can someone tell me how am I getting this error here?<br>\nI didn't change imports at all except the import from Mathlib.Data.Set.Defs to Mathlib.Data.Set.Operations.</p>\n<p>I don't see how that one gets Topology into linear algebra.</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">Modules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">starting</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">LinearAlgebra</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">are</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">not</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">allowed</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">to</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">modules</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">starting</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">with</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">This</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">module</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">depends</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">on</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Basic</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousMap</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Homeomorph</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Defs</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Constructions</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">SumProd</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Constructions</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">NhdsWithin</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">ContinuousOn</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bases</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Compactness</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Bases</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Sets</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Opens</span><span class=\"o\">,</span>\n<span class=\"n\">which</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">is</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">imported</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Topology</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">Sets</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">OpenCover</s